  "contentPlaintext": "<bold>Team Charter & Agreements</bold>\nThis document establishes the governance, communication protocols, and operational standards for the project team. All members must review, agree, and sign this charter.\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Team Roster & Roles\n3. Communication & Logistics Protocols\n4. Version Control & Development Standards\n5. Conflict Resolution Framework\n6. Document Sign-Off & Accountability\n<bold>2. Team Roster & Roles</bold>\nName\nWorkspace Role\nCore Technical Focus\nSecondary Responsibility\n<italic>[Student 1]</italic>\nProject Lead (Manager)\nSystem Architecture / Integration\nSupervisor Liaison\n<italic>[Student 2]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nFrontend Architecture / UI-UX\nTechnical Documentation\n<italic>[Student 3]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nBackend Infrastructure / API\nDatabase Administration\n<italic>[Student 4]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nDevOps / Testing Automation\nQA Lead\n<italic>[Student 5]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nMachine Learning / Core Logic\nData Pipeline\n<bold>3. Communication & Logistics Protocols</bold>\n<bold>Formal Channels</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Primary Communications</textStyle></bold>: [e.g., Slack / Microsoft Teams / Discord] for daily operational syncs.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Workspace Portal</textStyle></bold>: CollabSphere for task tracking, document reviews, and official submissions.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Emergency Channel</textStyle></bold>: [e.g., WhatsApp / Signal / Phone calls] for blocks requiring responses under 3 hours.\n<bold>Response Time SLAs</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Working Days (Mon - Fri)</textStyle></bold>: Maximum <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">4 hours</textStyle></bold> response time for direct mentions.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Weekends (Sat - Sun)</textStyle></bold>: Maximum <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">12 hours</textStyle></bold> response time for project-critical blocks.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">General Announcements</textStyle></bold>: Must be acknowledged with a reaction or reply within <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">24 hours</textStyle></bold>.\n<bold>Meeting Rhythms</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Weekly Internal Sync</textStyle></bold>: Every [Day] at [Time] via [Platform] to review task boards and blockers.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Supervisor Review</textStyle></bold>: Every [Day] at [Time] to present project status updates.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Attendance Policy</textStyle></bold>: Attendance is mandatory. Absences require a notice minimum <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">24 hours</textStyle></bold> in advance.\n<bold>4. Version Control & Development Standards</bold>\n<bold>Git Branching Strategy</bold>\n<code>main</code> / <code>production</code>: Stable, deployable code. Code must never be pushed directly here.\n<code>develop</code> / <code>staging</code>: Integration branch for functional feature testing.\n<code>feature/issue-ticket-*</code>: Individual isolated working branches named after active tasks.\n<bold>Pull Request (PR) Requirements</bold>\nAll PRs require an absolute minimum of <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">two peer approvals</textStyle></bold> before integration into <code>develop</code>.\nCI/CD automated pipeline builds and test suites must pass 100% successfully.\nThe author must resolve all review blockages and comments before merging code.\n<bold>5. Conflict Resolution Framework</bold>\nIf internal professional disagreements or performance anomalies occur, the team will follow this explicit escalation model:\n[ Step 1: Internal Peer Sync ] ➔ [ Step 2: Project Lead Mediation ] ➔ [ Step 3: Supervisor Intervention ]\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Step 1: Direct Internal Peer Sync</textStyle></bold>: Involved parties schedule a private meeting to objective-map the friction point and find a common design compromise.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Step 2: Project Lead Mediation</textStyle></bold>: If unresolved within <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">48 hours</textStyle></bold>, the Project Lead reviews arguments against objective constraints (deadlines, faculty rubrics) and issues a binding decision.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Step 3: Supervisor Intervention</textStyle></bold>: If non-cooperation or missed task performance persists across two milestones, the issue escalates to the Supervisor for grading adjustment or separation.\n<bold>6. Document Sign-Off & Accountability</bold>\nBy printing your name below, you commit to upholding these execution agreements, performance metrics, and communication response windows.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Project Lead Signature</textStyle></bold>: _____________________ (Date: __________)\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Student 2 Signature</textStyle></bold>: _____________________ (Date: __________)\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Student 3 Signature</textStyle></bold>: _____________________ (Date: __________)\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Student 4 Signature</textStyle></bold>: _____________________ (Date: __________)\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Student 5 Signature</textStyle></bold>: _____________________ (Date: __________)",
  "blocks": []
}